  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During 2025, Viet Nam experienced a series of severe and compounding climate-related disasters, including Typhoons Bualoi, Matmo, Fengshen, and Kalmaegi, which triggered widespread flooding, landslides, and extensive damage to housing, infrastructure, livelihoods, and essential services across multiple regions. The cumulative impacts of these successive events disproportionately affected vulnerable populations, particularly in the Central Highlands and Northern mountainous provinces, including G</narrative>
